=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: pc15
diagnosis_text:
**Affected component:** The default route (default gateway) on pc15's eth0 interface.

**Mechanism:** PC15 has its default gateway set to `172.18.51.250`, an address that does not exist anywhere on the 172.18.51.0/24 subnet. Whenever pc15 needs to forward a packet to any off-subnet destination — including the wireless VLAN 50 segment (172.18.50.x) where Laptop4 lives — it attempts an ARP resolution for 172.18.51.250. No device on the subnet holds that IP, so ARP fails (kernel marks the neighbor entry `FAILED`) and pc15 itself generates an ICMP "Destination Host Unreachable" response. This is why traffic that stays on-subnet (pc15 ↔ pc16/17/18) still works: those packets are on-link and never consult the gateway.

**Localization:** The fault is exclusively on pc15. The three VLAN 51 peers — pc16, pc17, pc18 — all have their default gateway correctly set to `172.18.51.254`, which is the active upstream router interface, and they all reach Laptop4 (172.18.50.14) with 0% loss.

**Root cause:** PC15's default gateway is misconfigured as `172.18.51.250` instead of the correct `172.18.51.254`, making it unable to route any inter-VLAN or inter-subnet traffic.

**Fix:** Correct pc15's default route by removing the spurious entry (`ip route del default via 172.18.51.250`) and adding the correct one (`ip route add default via 172.18.51.254`), or update the persistent network configuration file that provisioned the wrong gateway value.
=== END ===